    "text": "Let P = AB be a finite p-group factorized by an abelian subgroup A and\na class-two subgroup B. Suppose, if necessary, A ∩ B = 1. Then is it true that\n⟨A, [B, B]⟩ = AB0 , where B0 is an abelian subgroup of B?             E. Jabara",
